  "phrases": [
    {
      "id": "hook",
      "text": "A round manhole cover can do something surprisingly important: stay above the manhole.",
      "start": 0.071,
      "end": 4.529,
      "wordRange": [
        0,
        12
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cannot-fall",
      "text": "A circular cover cannot fall straight through its own circular opening.",
      "start": 4.881,
      "end": 8.222,
      "wordRange": [
        13,
        23
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "other-shapes",
      "text": "With some other shapes, orientation can become a problem.",
      "start": 8.537,
      "end": 11.18,
      "wordRange": [
        24,
        32
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "other-wins",
      "text": "Round covers are also easy to roll, don't need to be rotated into one exact alignment, and fit naturally over circular shafts.",
      "start": 11.561,
      "end": 18.544,
      "wordRange": [
        33,
        54
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "engineers",
      "text": "So engineers didn't choose the circle because it looks nice. They chose a shape that quietly solves several annoying problems at once,",
      "start": 18.887,
      "end": 25.4,
      "wordRange": [
        55,
        76
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "payoff",
      "text": "which is basically engineering's favorite way of showing off.",
      "start": 25.703,
      "end": 28.204,
      "wordRange": [
        77,
        85
      ]
    }
  ],
